a/input.csv and match, and the two-sided Fisher exact p-value of 0.039126 is correct for that 2x2 table.\",\"The absence of within-unit repeated measurements is demonstrated, not just asserted: workflow/analysis.py raises an error if pond_id values are duplicated before tallying, and the report's Design and Reading sections state that every pond_id appears in exactly one row so no pond contributes more than a single outcome to the table.\",\"The Fisher exact test is applied to counts of independent ponds with one trial per pond, matching the data description's statement that the 24 rows are 24 independent units; the auxiliary columns (volume, stocking density, temperature) are pond-level covariates, not repeated measurements.\",\"No minted authority lock was shown, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["The declared independent-unit column pond_id is consistent with the frozen data: all 24 values (P01-P24) are unique, so each pond contributes exactly one row and one trial, with 12 ponds in each treatment arm (shaded and open) and no unit appearing in both arms.","The contingency counts in the report (shaded 9 persisted / 3 collapsed; open 3 persisted / 9 collapsed) were recomputed from data/input.csv and match, and the two-sided Fisher exact p-value of 0.039126 is correct for that 2x2 table.","The absence of within-unit repeated measurements is demonstrated, not just asserted: workflow/analysis.py raises an error if pond_id values are duplicated before tallying, and the report's Design and Reading sections state that every pond_id appears in exactly one row so no pond contributes more than a single outcome to the table.","The Fisher exact test is applied to counts of independent ponds with one trial per pond, matching the data description's statement that the 24 rows are 24 independent units; the auxiliary columns (volume, stocking density, temperature) are pond-level covariates, not repeated measurements.","No minted authority lock was shown, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":6552,"ttft_stream_ms":2127,"time_to_request_ms":12,"type":"result","duration_ms":15624,"uuid":"255c3d64-6ced-4ce4-a9bb-c9c2696871ec"}
